This is the fourth sheet of the series; the circled '(4)' is the sheet number and '9' is the archive page. It fixes notation for the dual pair A^∧ = presheaves A^op→Ens and A^∨ = covariant functors A→Ens (copresheaves). The previous pages work with ℱ(Top(A)) = A^∨ and use the same pair of symbols.

The pairing ⟨Φ_*, Φ^*⟩_A, for Φ_* ∈ A^∧ and Φ^* ∈ A^∨, is in all likelihood the tensor product of functors (coend): Φ_* ⊗_A Φ^* = ∫^a Φ_*(a) × Φ^*(a), a set. This is the 'evaluation' of a presheaf against a copresheaf.

For a functor f: A → B there are four functors:
- f^* : B^∧ → A^∧, restriction of presheaves;
- f_! : A^∧ → B^∧, its left adjoint (left Kan extension);
- f^{∘*} : B^∨ → A^∨, restriction of copresheaves (composition with f^∘);
- f^∘_! : A^∨ → B^∨, left Kan extension of copresheaves.

The boxed formulas are the two adjunction-type ('projection formula / reciprocity') isomorphisms between these pairings:
(1) ⟨Φ_*, f^{∘*}Ψ^*⟩_A ≃ ⟨f_!Φ_*, Ψ^*⟩_B;
(2) ⟨f^*Ψ_*, Φ^*⟩_A ≃ ⟨Ψ_*, f^∘_!Φ^*⟩_B.
That is, f_! and f^{∘*} are transposes of each other with respect to the pairings, and likewise f^* and f^∘_!.

The role in the manuscript is to set up the duality between the topos Â and the 'dual' category A^∨, seen as functions on, or points of, Top(A). The previous page deals with Top(A) → X → Top(B), with φ_*(F) for F ∈ A^∨ and ψ^*(G) for G ∈ B^∨. Under this duality, push-forward and pull-back of 'functional correspondences' are mutually adjoint for the canonical pairing. This prepares the next page, which builds the category of triples (H_*, H^*, α) from a fully faithful embedding A ⊂ B.
